{
  "id": "mach-bands",
  "term": "Mach bands",
  "definition": "Mach bands are a visual illusion in which faint bright and dark stripes appear near changes in luminance, such as at the edges of a luminance trapezoid. They are used to study brightness perception and spatial vision, and have been explained as arising from early visual processes including local response normalization.",
